00:01:38.648 --> 00:01:41.108
they don't have the money
to be able to pay you

00:01:41.108 --> 00:01:44.866
for what you do, and
even if they do value it,

00:01:44.866 --> 00:01:46.637
they value your experience and expertise,

00:01:46.637 --> 00:01:49.022
they don't actually have
the money to pay you for it.

00:01:49.022 --> 00:01:51.927
There'll be other people
who have the money,

00:01:51.927 --> 00:01:54.698
but they don't value what you do enough,

00:01:54.698 --> 00:01:57.035
and so those aren't ideal clients either.

00:01:57.035 --> 00:01:59.198
Instead of wasting your energy trying to

00:01:59.198 --> 00:02:02.100
convince people to spend
more money with you

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.647
or that you can provide
the value, I would rather

00:02:04.647 --> 00:02:09.050
invest my time prospecting and
working with ideal clients.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:12.048
And so I don't really try to bring clients

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:14.803
aboard with value-based pricing.

00:02:14.803 --> 00:02:16.515
I try to go out and find the clients

00:02:16.515 --> 00:02:18.381
that are already attuned to it,

00:02:18.381 --> 00:02:20.052
and work with those people instead.

00:02:20.052 --> 00:02:23.421
(upbeat music)

00:02:23.421 --> 00:02:25.672
So that takes us to step
two, which is define

00:02:25.672 --> 00:02:27.433
what an ideal client looks like.

00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:29.664
So one, they have to
have the budget, right,

00:02:29.664 --> 00:02:30.984
whatever range you're in.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:33.021
So if, for example,
when I deal with brands,

00:02:33.021 --> 00:02:35.771
my first brand deal was for $500.

00:02:36.672 --> 00:02:39.808
$500 to write a blog post, and I ended up

00:02:39.808 --> 00:02:42.239
over delivering, doing
great work for them.

00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:45.069
And this is a great example
of I carried them so far,

00:02:45.069 --> 00:02:49.319
so I started with $500,
and then we moved it to 750

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:51.476
or something and then 1,000 and then 1,250

00:02:51.476 --> 00:02:54.001
and then 1,500, and I moved them from $500

00:02:54.001 --> 00:02:57.135
to $1,500 for each post that I was doing,

00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:58.725
but that was their cap.

00:02:58.725 --> 00:03:00.895
That was their limit,
and I was bringing them

00:03:00.895 --> 00:03:03.783
more than $1,500 worth of value every time

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:06.668
I did it, 'cause I put in
so much work and effort.

00:03:06.668 --> 00:03:08.507
So eventually, I had to leave them.

00:03:08.507 --> 00:03:11.665
Instead of trying to bring
that brand with me up,

00:03:11.665 --> 00:03:15.502
I left them, and I brought
on bigger brand deals.

00:03:15.502 --> 00:03:18.326
And so understand what is an ideal client.

00:03:18.326 --> 00:03:19.464
What do they look like for you?

00:03:19.464 --> 00:03:22.165
What budget do they need to have?

00:03:22.165 --> 00:03:23.491
What values do they need to have?

00:03:23.491 --> 00:03:25.685
If you understand your one
word, and you understand

00:03:25.685 --> 00:03:28.844
what values they're looking
for, having a good mash.

00:03:28.844 --> 00:03:30.622
Most of the brands that want to work

00:03:30.622 --> 00:03:33.358
with me I say no to, because
we're not in alignment.

00:03:33.358 --> 00:03:35.787
They just want to sell you guys stuff,

00:03:35.787 --> 00:03:37.225
because they don't actually care much

00:03:37.225 --> 00:03:39.016
about entrepreneurs,
and if you don't believe

00:03:39.016 --> 00:03:40.317
in entrepreneurs, you're not going to be

00:03:40.317 --> 00:03:41.470
a good fit for this channel.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:42.869
I don't want to do a
deal with you, even if

00:03:42.869 --> 00:03:45.081
you throw tons of cash at me, because it's

00:03:45.081 --> 00:03:46.869
not going to be a good long-term fit.

00:03:46.869 --> 00:03:49.275
We're just going to fight
because of values differences.

00:03:49.275 --> 00:03:51.070
So understanding the clients
that have the budget,

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.685
clients that have the
values, clients that are

00:03:52.685 --> 00:03:54.249
doing the work that is
meaningful and important to you,

00:03:54.249 --> 00:03:56.454
setting that list of what an ideal client

00:03:56.454 --> 00:03:59.001
looks like for you, being
able to identify them,

00:03:59.001 --> 00:04:01.737
will help you be able to do
out and get them on board.

00:04:01.737 --> 00:04:04.320
(upbeat music)

00:04:05.217 --> 00:04:07.237
Tip number three is prove your value.

00:04:07.237 --> 00:04:10.379
So once you've found who
these ideal targets are,

00:04:10.379 --> 00:04:12.229
you've created your criteria and you've

00:04:12.229 --> 00:04:13.663
identified who these people are or who

00:04:13.663 --> 00:04:16.121
these brands are or companies are,

00:04:16.121 --> 00:04:18.530
I love starting off with a small deal

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.620
and then finding a way to make it bigger.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:21.577
Prove your value.

00:04:21.577 --> 00:04:23.653
If nobody knows who you
are, you don't have a name,

00:04:23.653 --> 00:04:25.314
you don't have a reputation, you look like

00:04:25.314 --> 00:04:27.780
everybody else, prove your value.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.060
If you get in with a low price, with a low

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.324
amount of work, right,
like some small project,

00:04:32.324 --> 00:04:34.508
then it's easier to get
a yes, and it's easier

00:04:34.508 --> 00:04:36.372
to continue on with them.

00:04:36.372 --> 00:04:40.250
And so understand that
whatever it is that you do,

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.533
a company that you want to work with,

00:04:41.533 --> 00:04:43.942
they probably already have
some kind of existing supplier.

00:04:43.942 --> 00:04:46.106
They're already working with
people who look like you.

00:04:46.106 --> 00:04:48.519
They're working with your
competition in some respect.

00:04:48.519 --> 00:04:49.957
And so if you go in and try to pitch,

00:04:49.957 --> 00:04:53.481
taking on this huge deal, one, it involves

00:04:53.481 --> 00:04:55.851
kicking out your
competition, who they have

00:04:55.851 --> 00:04:57.697
an established working relationship with,

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:59.859
and a big deal involves more people

00:04:59.859 --> 00:05:02.036
at that company to make a decision.

00:05:02.036 --> 00:05:04.428
And so the bigger it is,
the more complicated it is,

00:05:04.428 --> 00:05:06.506
the more steps involved, the less likely

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:08.071
you are to get a yes.

00:05:08.071 --> 00:05:10.502
What I'd rather do is go into a company

00:05:10.502 --> 00:05:11.902
and ask where they're unhappy.

00:05:11.902 --> 00:05:15.402
Find one small scenario
where they are unhappy.

00:05:15.402 --> 00:05:17.884
So if you're doing website
design, as an example,

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.369
instead of trying to take over an entire

00:05:19.369 --> 00:05:21.881
company's website, find one landing page.

00:05:21.881 --> 00:05:25.264
Like what one landing
page are you unhappy with.

00:05:25.264 --> 00:05:26.762
Just give me one thing that you're unhappy

00:05:26.762 --> 00:05:28.605
with, that your current
supplier is not doing

00:05:28.605 --> 00:05:30.209
a good job with, for whatever reason,

00:05:30.209 --> 00:05:32.400
no judgment against them,
you're just unhappy with.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.105
Let me prove my value to you.

00:05:35.105 --> 00:05:38.278
And charge them a reasonable
price to do one small project.

00:05:38.278 --> 00:05:39.881
Something that is easy
for them to give to you

00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:41.983
that one person has to make a decision on,

00:05:41.983 --> 00:05:43.516
and you've got your budget to work with,

00:05:43.516 --> 00:05:44.858
even though it's a small one.

00:05:44.858 --> 00:05:46.891
And then over-deliver like crazy.

00:05:46.891 --> 00:05:48.109
Give them so much value.

00:05:48.109 --> 00:05:49.772
Be their favorite supplier.

00:05:49.772 --> 00:05:52.787
Be the person that then,
whoever you worked with,

00:05:52.787 --> 00:05:54.457
saying these guys do such great work,

00:05:54.457 --> 00:05:56.048
we should give them more business.

00:05:56.048 --> 00:05:57.905
If you do that work, you won't even have

00:05:57.905 --> 00:06:00.649
to pitch the other
business, getting the whole

00:06:00.649 --> 00:06:01.919
website, because they're
going to be fighting

00:06:01.919 --> 00:06:04.785
for you to have that business.

00:06:04.785 --> 00:06:05.743
Does it make sense?

00:06:05.743 --> 00:06:07.092
The more entrenched you are,

00:06:07.092 --> 00:06:08.275
the more value you're providing,

00:06:08.275 --> 00:06:10.089
the tighter you build that relationship,

00:06:10.089 --> 00:06:13.941
giving them so much more
value than the competition is,

00:06:13.941 --> 00:06:16.263
they're going to fight
to give you more work

00:06:16.263 --> 00:06:18.920
because they love working with you.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:19.985
And so, too often, people come in

00:06:19.985 --> 00:06:22.289
and they pitch these huge ideas

00:06:22.289 --> 00:06:23.687
when nobody knows who they are,

00:06:23.687 --> 00:06:25.363
and it's just so complicated a deal

00:06:25.363 --> 00:06:26.874
and takes too many steps that you're

00:06:26.874 --> 00:06:27.921
not going to get a yes.

00:06:27.921 --> 00:06:30.538
Well, if you go in with some
easy-to-say-yes-to decision,

00:06:30.538 --> 00:06:32.966
and then you over deliver like crazy,

00:06:32.966 --> 00:06:34.989
you're going to get more
and more and more work.

00:06:34.989 --> 00:06:37.799
But make sure it's with an ideal client.

00:06:37.799 --> 00:06:40.382
(upbeat music)

00:06:41.359 --> 00:06:44.980
Tip number four is figure out
the why of your customers.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.361
This is super important.

00:06:46.361 --> 00:06:48.625
In a competitive world,
where a lot of people

00:06:48.625 --> 00:06:50.831
are trying to under-price each other,

00:06:50.831 --> 00:06:53.369
the ultimate way to
win over your customers

00:06:53.369 --> 00:06:55.801
is by understanding why
they're coming to you

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:57.090
in the first place.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.739
So here's what happens at our school.

00:06:58.739 --> 00:07:01.440
Whenever clients come
into TDS, one of the first

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.452
questions they ask is
how much are the classes.

00:07:03.452 --> 00:07:06.522
What I make sure to do is ask them why

00:07:06.522 --> 00:07:09.062
they're interested, before
we even talk about pricing.

00:07:09.062 --> 00:07:10.773
If I can figure out their why,

00:07:10.773 --> 00:07:12.790
whether it's to make friends, to be more

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.887
comfortable with their
body, whatever it is,

00:07:14.887 --> 00:07:18.067
I can tailor my conversation around that.

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:21.215
And what happens then is, price
doesn't become as important,

00:07:21.215 --> 00:07:23.705
because, ultimately, people will pay a lot

00:07:23.705 --> 00:07:26.528
more for a product that
addresses their needs,

00:07:26.528 --> 00:07:28.305
their deep-down desires.

00:07:28.305 --> 00:07:30.652
So if you spend a couple extra minutes

00:07:30.652 --> 00:07:32.513
to figure out the why of your customers,

00:07:32.513 --> 00:07:35.290
you'll be able to charge
them what you're worth

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.676
and, ultimately, have loyal customers.

00:07:37.676 --> 00:07:40.259
(upbeat music)

00:07:41.298 --> 00:07:43.518
Number five is over-deliver
like crazy, and I touched

00:07:43.518 --> 00:07:45.340
on it in point number three.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:48.235
It's really important that
once you get in the door

00:07:48.235 --> 00:07:49.990
that you are doing everything you can

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.589
to be remembered and
just providing so much

00:07:52.589 --> 00:07:54.171
insane value to help them.

00:07:54.171 --> 00:07:56.056
And what you want to think about is what

00:07:56.056 --> 00:07:58.551
skills do I have, what people do I know

00:07:58.551 --> 00:08:01.339
that can help make this
project just so much better?

00:08:01.339 --> 00:08:03.739
And so, as an example,
things that I've done.

00:08:03.739 --> 00:08:06.354
In that first blog post
that I had $500 for,

00:08:06.354 --> 00:08:08.930
my very first brand
deal, all they wanted was

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:12.362
300 words for a blog post that they're

00:08:12.362 --> 00:08:14.029
going to post on their site.

00:08:14.029 --> 00:08:17.383
And so I didn't just write 300
words and give them content,

00:08:17.383 --> 00:08:20.981
I wrote 1,500 words, something like that,

00:08:20.981 --> 00:08:22.799
and I give them the
longest article that they

00:08:22.799 --> 00:08:24.038
ever had for their blog.

00:08:24.038 --> 00:08:27.507
I made a video that was
custom for that post.

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:29.381
I promoted it to my newsletter list

00:08:29.381 --> 00:08:31.448
and let my audience
know to go check it out.

00:08:31.448 --> 00:08:33.676
And they hired me, and they hired nine

00:08:33.676 --> 00:08:36.278
other influencers, so
there was 10 of us total

00:08:36.278 --> 00:08:38.978
for this project, and I was the only one

00:08:38.978 --> 00:08:40.893
that they picked to continue on with.

00:08:40.893 --> 00:08:44.490
Why, because my content got more impact,

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.666
got more results, more
engagement, more views

00:08:46.666 --> 00:08:48.590
than all of the other nine combined,

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.941
because I gave them so much more value.

00:08:50.941 --> 00:08:53.669
And so any time a
customer's asking for this,

00:08:53.669 --> 00:08:55.193
you want to give them this.

00:08:55.193 --> 00:08:57.783
But then you also want
to give them more, right?

00:08:57.783 --> 00:08:59.952
Using your skills, your
resources, your connections,

00:08:59.952 --> 00:09:02.420
your knowledge to give them
more than what they asked for.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:03.666
That's how you over deliver.

00:09:03.666 --> 00:09:05.533
That's how you can start
raising your prices.

00:09:05.533 --> 00:09:06.854
That's how you can start getting more

00:09:06.854 --> 00:09:09.036
business within the organization.

00:09:09.036 --> 00:09:11.059
And so maybe you know somebody that can

00:09:11.059 --> 00:09:13.401
help that company out,
maybe you can connect

00:09:13.401 --> 00:09:14.854
two people together,
two companies together,

00:09:14.854 --> 00:09:17.687
where there's an interaction
that's mutually beneficial.

00:09:17.687 --> 00:09:19.908
Maybe you can provide
a video or go longer.

00:09:19.908 --> 00:09:21.937
Always think about the baker's dozen.

00:09:21.937 --> 00:09:23.514
13 is the baker's dozen.

00:09:23.514 --> 00:09:26.930
So you buy 12 of something,
you get the 13th one for free.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:30.719
What can you add in that is
unexpected value for them?

00:09:30.719 --> 00:09:32.243
Help them in any way possible.

00:09:32.243 --> 00:09:33.729
Cover them on your website.

00:09:33.729 --> 00:09:35.841
Be a testimonial for them on LinkedIn.

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:36.989
Whatever it is.

00:09:36.989 --> 00:09:37.924
Showcase their stuff.

00:09:37.924 --> 00:09:39.913
Follow them on Twitter
and retweet their things

00:09:39.913 --> 00:09:41.575
and be engaged, because I guarantee you,

00:09:41.575 --> 00:09:44.308
no other supplier they're
working with is doing this.

00:09:44.308 --> 00:09:45.992
And this is your chance to stand out.

00:09:45.992 --> 00:09:48.358
You get some small,
easy-to-say-yes-to deal,

00:09:48.358 --> 00:09:50.788
and you provide just so much value to them

00:09:50.788 --> 00:09:53.707
that they want to find
ways, they will fight

00:09:53.707 --> 00:09:56.359
for ways to continue working with you.

00:09:56.359 --> 00:09:58.942
(upbeat music)

00:09:59.998 --> 00:10:02.451
Tip number six is keep
increasing your pricing.

00:10:02.451 --> 00:10:04.599
So I'm a big fan as you get better,

00:10:04.599 --> 00:10:06.768
as you understand how to add more value,

00:10:06.768 --> 00:10:08.602
as you improve your skillsets and you

00:10:08.602 --> 00:10:10.103
can bring more value to the table,

00:10:10.103 --> 00:10:12.396
that you continue to
increase your pricing.

00:10:12.396 --> 00:10:14.431
The way I do it on my YouTube channel,

00:10:14.431 --> 00:10:16.006
as an example, since you
guys are watching is,

00:10:16.006 --> 00:10:19.206
I can only work with so
many brands at a time.

00:10:19.206 --> 00:10:21.590
And usually I'll work on annual deals.

00:10:21.590 --> 00:10:23.385
So a brand works with me, it will be

00:10:23.385 --> 00:10:24.603
for at least a year.

00:10:24.603 --> 00:10:26.222
And because I can only work with so many

00:10:26.222 --> 00:10:29.836
brands at a time, every
time I get a new brand,

00:10:29.836 --> 00:10:31.316
I increase the price.

00:10:31.316 --> 00:10:32.978
There's limited supply.

00:10:32.978 --> 00:10:34.030
We can only do so many.

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:36.062
So okay, for you it's this, and now,

00:10:36.062 --> 00:10:38.006
next time it's this, next time it's this.

00:10:38.006 --> 00:10:40.174
And I did the same thing
before I was doing YouTube,

00:10:40.174 --> 00:10:41.671
when I was just having my website and my

00:10:41.671 --> 00:10:43.565
blog and my newsletter list.

00:10:43.565 --> 00:10:46.460
I would send one newsletter out a week,

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:49.230
maximum, that would be in
partnership with a brand.

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:51.626
So there's only four a
month that could happen.

00:10:51.626 --> 00:10:54.540
So I'd sell the first one at $1,500

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.423
and the second one maybe at $1,500.

00:10:56.423 --> 00:10:57.813
Now, my space is getting limited.

00:10:57.813 --> 00:11:00.303
So okay, the next one's at $1,750,

00:11:00.303 --> 00:11:01.705
and the next one's at $2,000.

00:11:01.705 --> 00:11:03.577
And if somebody falls
off, then the next one's

00:11:03.577 --> 00:11:04.939
going to be at $2,250.

00:11:04.939 --> 00:11:07.232
So as your supply goes down,

00:11:07.232 --> 00:11:08.939
you start increasing your prices.

00:11:08.939 --> 00:11:11.709
As your value goes up, as you know more,

00:11:11.709 --> 00:11:13.248
you can bring more to your clients,

00:11:13.248 --> 00:11:15.129
you start increasing your prices.

00:11:15.129 --> 00:11:17.533
Where a lot of times,
entrepreneurs just stay stuck

00:11:17.533 --> 00:11:20.233
in the same zone for many years charging

00:11:20.233 --> 00:11:22.011
the same price, even
though they're bringing

00:11:22.011 --> 00:11:23.573
way, way, way more value.

00:11:23.573 --> 00:11:26.250
As you bring more value, you start raising

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:27.803
your prices alongside it.

00:11:27.803 --> 00:11:31.123
(upbeat music)

00:11:31.123 --> 00:11:32.575
And tip number seven, this is one of my

00:11:32.575 --> 00:11:35.146
favorite, is to be a thought leader.

00:11:35.146 --> 00:11:36.989
If you are so great at what you do,

00:11:36.989 --> 00:11:38.511
showcase your expertise.

00:11:38.511 --> 00:11:40.109
Be a thought leader so that people will

00:11:40.109 --> 00:11:43.204
find you, so you are not out having to do

00:11:43.204 --> 00:11:45.848
cold emails or cold tweets or cold calls

00:11:45.848 --> 00:11:49.338
or go to events and
congresses and conventions

00:11:49.338 --> 00:11:50.682
to try to make connections.

00:11:50.682 --> 00:11:54.056
Be a thought leader to
have people find you.

00:11:54.056 --> 00:11:55.616
See, when people hire thought leaders,

00:11:55.616 --> 00:11:56.781
they're willing to pay more.

00:11:56.781 --> 00:11:58.306
If they're bringing on
somebody who they think

00:11:58.306 --> 00:12:01.247
is the expert at this
field, they're going to

00:12:01.247 --> 00:12:02.370
be willing to pay more.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.919
They're seeking you out
because you are the leader.

00:12:05.919 --> 00:12:07.537
If somebody's only going to hire somebody

00:12:07.537 --> 00:12:09.649
based on price, they're not going to look

00:12:09.649 --> 00:12:12.066
at who's speaking at these events,

00:12:12.066 --> 00:12:14.467
who's writing the white
papers, who's being

00:12:14.467 --> 00:12:16.968
interviewed on the
different YouTube channels.

00:12:16.968 --> 00:12:18.849
It's just a different mindset.

00:12:18.849 --> 00:12:21.016
The people who want the value,

00:12:21.016 --> 00:12:22.621
the people who want fast results

00:12:22.621 --> 00:12:24.813
are people who appreciate the people

00:12:24.813 --> 00:12:27.238
who are bringing the results to them,

00:12:27.238 --> 00:12:28.842
they seek those people out.

00:12:28.842 --> 00:12:30.916
And they pay premium
dollars for those people.

00:12:30.916 --> 00:12:34.023
So the way to get that
is to expose yourself.

00:12:34.023 --> 00:12:34.856
Be a thought leader.

00:12:34.856 --> 00:12:35.689
Share your opinions.

00:12:35.689 --> 00:12:37.143
Share your expertise.

00:12:37.143 --> 00:12:39.912
Anytime a reporter is
talking about a subject

00:12:39.912 --> 00:12:43.417
that is in your field, write
to them and give your opinion.

00:12:43.417 --> 00:12:44.828
Share your expertise.

00:12:44.828 --> 00:12:46.240
You could be a resource for them.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.243
Reporters are always looking for people

00:12:48.243 --> 00:12:50.154
to comment on articles.

00:12:50.154 --> 00:12:52.055
They always need industry expertise.

00:12:52.055 --> 00:12:52.959
That could be you.

00:12:52.959 --> 00:12:55.487
That's how I got into New York Times

00:12:55.487 --> 00:12:57.605
and all these other
publications and all these

00:12:57.605 --> 00:13:00.269
lists of speakers and thought leaders

00:13:00.269 --> 00:13:04.514
and SEO experts and social
media experts to follow,

00:13:04.514 --> 00:13:07.488
because I did a lot of work
connecting with reporters.

00:13:07.488 --> 00:13:08.585
Put out great content.

00:13:08.585 --> 00:13:09.724
Start a YouTube channel.

00:13:09.724 --> 00:13:11.451
Start a Twitter account.

00:13:11.451 --> 00:13:13.301
Whatever it is that your expertise is,

00:13:13.301 --> 00:13:15.303
you'd rather write,
you'd rather make video,

00:13:15.303 --> 00:13:17.478
you'd rather do audio, you need to spend

00:13:17.478 --> 00:13:20.420
time being a media company and sharing

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:23.532
your expertise to be
seen as a thought leader

00:13:23.532 --> 00:13:26.179
so that people will find you, and you can

00:13:26.179 --> 00:13:27.411
start turning people down.

00:13:27.411 --> 00:13:29.098
When I look at brand deals,

00:13:29.098 --> 00:13:31.375
there's platforms out there where you

00:13:31.375 --> 00:13:34.453
can bid on working with a brand, right?

00:13:34.453 --> 00:13:36.721
Famebit is one, as an example.

00:13:36.721 --> 00:13:39.125
Brands will post a
deal, say we have $1,000

00:13:39.125 --> 00:13:40.861
to work on this deal,
and all these different

00:13:40.861 --> 00:13:42.508
creators will bid on it.

00:13:42.508 --> 00:13:44.620
You have no leverage in that situation.

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:47.217
You're one of hundreds of creators bidding

00:13:47.217 --> 00:13:50.807
on a project, and it's
just a race to the bottom.

00:13:50.807 --> 00:13:52.413
I'm willing to do it for this.

00:13:52.413 --> 00:13:53.908
I'm willing to throw in this for free.

00:13:53.908 --> 00:13:55.606
You compete against so many people,

00:13:55.606 --> 00:13:57.018
and the brand has all the power,

00:13:57.018 --> 00:13:59.415
where when I'm creating content,

00:13:59.415 --> 00:14:01.643
and the brands come to me,

00:14:01.643 --> 00:14:03.136
I'm the one who has the power.

00:14:03.136 --> 00:14:04.629
I'm the one who can set the pricing.

00:14:04.629 --> 00:14:06.480
I'm the one who can dictate the terms,

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:07.643
because they're coming to me.

00:14:07.643 --> 00:14:09.137
And so that's what I
want to create for you.

00:14:09.137 --> 00:14:10.786
I want people to come to you,

00:14:10.786 --> 00:14:13.224
to find you, to reach out to you,

00:14:13.224 --> 00:14:16.546
because you are the thought
leader expert in the field.

00:14:16.546 --> 00:14:18.020
And chances are you already know it.

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.414
If you're an entrepreneur, you should be

00:14:19.414 --> 00:14:20.247
good at what you do.

00:14:20.247 --> 00:14:21.960
You already have the
knowledge, but you're only

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.539
helping a select group of people,

00:14:23.539 --> 00:14:25.480
where if you're making that more public,

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:28.741
and you're sharing what's
already in here out there,

00:14:28.741 --> 00:14:30.532
you're going to attract people who value

00:14:30.532 --> 00:14:33.873
that expertise, and they'll
pay you top dollar for it.

00:14:33.873 --> 00:14:35.685
So those are my seven tips, seven ways

00:14:35.685 --> 00:14:38.300
on how to get clients aboard
with value-based pricing.

